# This repository is text with LF line endings, and a V compiler, a hex dump and a diff all
# agree on that. Leaving it to core.autocrlf means a fresh checkout can hand back CRLF, which
# `v fmt` then reports as unformatted while `git diff` shows nothing, because git normalises
# the difference away on the way out. That is a confusing failure to debug twice.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts are read as bytes. Normalising them would corrupt every offset in the file, which for a
# font is the difference between a table that parses and one that does not.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary